            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Bengali for to bring about, then the Bengali for gradually."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: সেদিন",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "সেদিন — sedin — \"that day; the other day\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "সেদিন বিকেলে হঠাৎ ঝড় এল। sedin bikele hôṭhāt jhôṛ elô. That day a storm blew up suddenly in the late afternoon."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "সেদিন (sedin) joins সে, 'that', to দিন, a day — Sanskrit dina (CDIAL 6328) — into one word: that day, the day the story is about. In talk it also means 'the other day', a few days ago."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
        },
