              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "পেরোনো — perono — \"to pass by; to go past\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "বছর পেরোল, কিন্তু রাজকুমার ফিরল না। bôchhôr perolô, kintu rājkumār phirlô nā. Years went by, but the prince did not return."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (he/she …): সেই নৌকা নদী পেরোল, sei noukā nôdī perolô."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "পেরোনো (perono) is usually explained as built on পার, 'the far bank' — Sanskrit pāra (CDIAL 8100) — with the verb ending: to get to the far side of a river, or of a stretch of time."
            }
          ]
        },
