            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Bengali for to go past, then the Bengali for in the course of time."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: স্মরণ করা",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "স্মরণ করা — smôrôn kôrā — \"to commemorate; to call to mind\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "আজ শহর সেই ভূমিকম্পের দিনটা স্মরণ করল। āj shôhôr sei bhūmikômper dinṭā smôrôn kôrlô. Today the city commemorated the day of that earthquake."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (he/she …): তিনি বাবাকে স্মরণ করলেন, tini bābāke smôrôn kôrlen."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "স্মরণ করা (smôrôn kôrā) puts Sanskrit smaraṇa, 'the act of remembering' (Monier-Williams), before করা. It is more formal than মনে রাখা and is the word for honouring a memory in public; স্মৃতি comes from the same root."
            }
          ]
        },
